 "comment": "Palutena's parts shown on demand (A10, scripts/p6/look_parts.py): each a model-part variant of an existing row drawing that row's list plus cut-out cards, two-sided. Corners are in the look's rest model space (y up, she faces +z; the battle camera sees her x axis as depth, so the cards lie across y and z). The wings (forward and down smash: SetModelPartID joint 6 part 1) are the kit's wing image (godwing, its full feathered wing, the island above it cleared), one card a side sweeping up and back from her shoulder blades. The halo (up air, the down taunt, the victory and select poses: joint 12 part 2) is an authored gold ring above her head, two crossed cards: one faces the battle camera, the other the select and Results cameras, which see her from the front. The light pillar is not a part any more (owner playtest 2026-10-14, round 2: her animation turned the hips row's cards behind her): it is an effect in her special file 2 (scripts/p6/p6_gate.py), its atlas look_parts.py's authored:pillar_burst. Owner p6i (\"Wings are not animating at all\"): the torso row's wings take three poses, its variants 1 (folded up and back), 2 (swept forward low: the forward smash's hit) and 3 (flapped down to the floor at her front and back: the down smash's), switched by the smash scripts at their frames as the torso turns and leans. (Cards hinged on the shoulder rows were tried: rows that draw nothing change the native owner's live root vector when shown, and those frames were declined.)",
